---
/**
 * The upload pipeline: a resumable upload that ends at object storage, and the
 * queue-driven stages that turn the file into a published video.
 *
 * Supplies only the shapes; `Figure` owns the `<svg>`, the accessible name and
 * description, the scroll frame and the caption. Every class comes from
 * Figure's drawing kit, so nothing here states a colour and both themes and
 * forced-colors mode come free.
 *
 * The claim the picture makes: the file bytes never pass through an
 * application server. That is why object storage is the accent box, why the
 * byte path is drawn as an arc that travels OVER the upload service rather
 * than through it, and why there is deliberately no connector at all between
 * the upload service and object storage. The 64 units of empty space between
 * those two boxes is the point of the drawing.
 *
 * LAYOUT NOTE: three lanes carry the flow between bands, and every one of them
 * runs through empty space. The byte arc rides above the top row at y=42, with
 * the chunked parts in flight drawn under it. The queue's second branch turns
 * down and left at y=296, in the strip between the metadata row and the
 * thumbnail box. The checks lane leaves the bottom rung of the ladder and runs
 * left at y=344, in the strip between the transcode row and the publish group,
 * passing to the right of the thumbnail box rather than across it. No
 * connector crosses a box.
 *
 * The thumbnail branch ends where the lesson's own pipeline sketch ends it, at
 * image storage: it is a consumer of the same event, not a stage the publish
 * transition waits behind, and drawing a rejoin would assert something the
 * lesson does not say. The checks lane starts at the LOWEST rung because that
 * is what the classifiers read (lesson step 6, "over the low rendition").
 *
 * TYPE TIERS: the ten pipeline stages are `.dg-label`; qualifying phrases,
 * states and lane names are `.dg-sub`; the literal request and the rung
 * identifiers are `.dg-mono`. `Live to viewers` is the one `.dg-legend`, and
 * the dashed group it names is what carries "not visible until publish":
 * everything drawn outside it happens while the video cannot be watched.
 */
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
  viewBox="0 0 700 516"
  title="Upload pipeline, session to published"
  description="A pipeline drawn in three bands, flowing left to right and top to bottom. In the top band a Creator client box, resumable session, PUT part 1 to n, sends a short arrow rightward into an Upload service box, session, auth, quota, never sees the bytes. A second line leaves the top of the Creator client, runs right along the top of the drawing above the Upload service, and ends with an arrowhead pointing down into the top of the highlighted Object storage box, the source file lands here, often the only copy. That line is labelled the file bytes go straight to storage, and three small chunks are drawn beneath its start, the parts in flight. There is no connector at all between the Upload service and Object storage. From the bottom of the Upload service an arrow runs down, then left, then down into a Metadata row box, state received, in the middle band. An arrow leads right from Metadata row into Event queue, source ready, and another arrow leads right from Event queue into Transcode workers, chunked, parallel, minutes, the slow stage. A dashed line drops from the bottom of Object storage into the top of Transcode workers, labelled reads the source. An arrow leads right from Transcode workers into a stack of four small boxes labelled 1080p, 720p, 480p and 360p, captioned rendition ladder. A second arrow leaves the bottom of Event queue, turns left and ends pointing down into a Thumbnails box, frames scored, to image storage, which has no outgoing connector. From the bottom rung of the ladder a line runs down, then left along an empty lane labelled the low rendition, then down into the bottom band, ending with an arrowhead on the top of a Validation and moderation box, abuse classifiers, copyright fingerprint match. An arrow leads right from that box into a dashed group named Live to viewers. The group holds two boxes joined by an arrow: Publish, state published, first moment it is visible, and CDN, pulled on the first view, nothing is pushed. Every stage drawn outside that dashed group happens while the video is not yet watchable."
  caption="The upload service authorises the session and never carries the file, which is why the byte path goes around it rather than through it. Everything after the queue is work the creator is not waiting on, and none of it is watchable: the video appears only when the publish transition moves it inside the group on the right."
  minWidth={640}
>
  <!-- The byte path: over the top of the upload service, not through it -->
  <text class="dg-sub" x="300" y="34" text-anchor="middle">
    the file bytes go straight to storage
  </text>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="74" y1="76" x2="74" y2="42"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="74" y1="42" x2="523" y2="42"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="523" y1="42" x2="523" y2="68"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="523,76 518,66 528,66"></polygon>

  <!-- The parts in flight -->
  <rect class="dg-box" x="100" y="50" width="22" height="16"></rect>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="128" y="50" width="22" height="16"></rect>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="156" y="50" width="22" height="16"></rect>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="186" y="63">parts in flight</text>

  <!-- The creator -->
  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="76" width="132" height="76"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="74" y="102" text-anchor="middle"
    >Creator client</text
  >
  <text class="dg-sub" x="74" y="122" text-anchor="middle">
    resumable session
  </text>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="74" y="142" text-anchor="middle">PUT part 1..n</text>

  <line class="dg-line" x1="140" y1="114" x2="188" y2="114"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="196,114 186,109 186,119"></polygon>

  <!-- The application tier: it authorises, and that is all it touches -->
  <rect class="dg-box" x="196" y="76" width="170" height="76"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="281" y="102" text-anchor="middle"
    >Upload service</text
  >
  <text class="dg-sub" x="281" y="122" text-anchor="middle">
    session, auth, quota
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="281" y="142" text-anchor="middle">
    never sees the bytes
  </text>

  <!-- Where the bytes land, and the only accent in the figure -->
  <rect class="dg-box dg-box--accent" x="430" y="76" width="186" height="76"
  ></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="523" y="102" text-anchor="middle"
    >Object storage</text
  >
  <text class="dg-sub" x="523" y="122" text-anchor="middle">
    the source file lands here
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="523" y="142" text-anchor="middle">
    often the only copy
  </text>

  <!-- The handoff: the service writes the row once the bytes are committed -->
  <line class="dg-line" x1="281" y1="152" x2="281" y2="176"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="281" y1="176" x2="81" y2="176"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="81" y1="176" x2="81" y2="200"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="81,208 76,198 86,198"></polygon>

  <!-- Workers read the source they did not receive -->
  <line class="dg-line dg-line--soft" x1="470" y1="152" x2="470" y2="192"
  ></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head dg-head--soft" points="470,202 465,192 475,192"
  ></polygon>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="462" y="172" text-anchor="end">reads the source</text>

  <!-- The pipeline half: a row, an event, and the fleet it feeds -->
  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="208" width="146" height="56"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="81" y="234" text-anchor="middle">Metadata row</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="81" y="254" text-anchor="middle">state: received</text
  >

  <line class="dg-line" x1="154" y1="236" x2="178" y2="236"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="186,236 176,231 176,241"></polygon>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="186" y="208" width="134" height="56"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="253" y="234" text-anchor="middle">Event queue</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="253" y="254" text-anchor="middle">source ready</text>

  <line class="dg-line" x1="320" y1="236" x2="352" y2="236"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="360,236 350,231 350,241"></polygon>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="360" y="202" width="160" height="68"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="440" y="224" text-anchor="middle">
    Transcode workers
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="440" y="242" text-anchor="middle">
    chunked, parallel
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="440" y="260" text-anchor="middle">
    minutes, the slow stage
  </text>

  <line class="dg-line" x1="520" y1="244" x2="540" y2="244"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="548,244 538,239 538,249"></polygon>

  <!-- The ladder: one rung first so the video can publish, then the rest -->
  <!-- Above the border, not on it: at y=182 the group's dashes ran through the
       ascenders. The other group in this drawing labels itself from the inside
       (.dg-legend); this one has four rungs and no room, so it labels itself
       from just outside. -->
  <text class="dg-sub" x="615" y="172" text-anchor="middle">
    rendition ladder
  </text>
  <rect class="dg-group" x="548" y="180" width="134" height="124"></rect>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="556" y="188" width="118" height="24"></rect>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="615" y="204" text-anchor="middle">1080p</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="556" y="216" width="118" height="24"></rect>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="615" y="232" text-anchor="middle">720p</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="556" y="244" width="118" height="24"></rect>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="615" y="260" text-anchor="middle">480p</text>
  <rect class="dg-box" x="556" y="272" width="118" height="24"></rect>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="615" y="288" text-anchor="middle">360p</text>

  <!-- The event's second consumer, down the strip beside the metadata row -->
  <line class="dg-line" x1="253" y1="264" x2="253" y2="296"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="253" y1="296" x2="79" y2="296"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="79" y1="296" x2="79" y2="308"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="79,316 74,306 84,306"></polygon>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="316" width="142" height="68"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="79" y="340" text-anchor="middle">Thumbnails</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="79" y="358" text-anchor="middle">frames scored</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="79" y="376" text-anchor="middle">
    to image storage
  </text>

  <!-- The lowest rung is what the classifiers read -->
  <line class="dg-line" x1="615" y1="296" x2="615" y2="344"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="615" y1="344" x2="176" y2="344"></line>
  <line class="dg-line" x1="176" y1="344" x2="176" y2="408"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="176,416 171,406 181,406"></polygon>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="400" y="336" text-anchor="middle">
    the low rendition
  </text>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="416" width="228" height="76"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="122" y="442" text-anchor="middle">
    Validation and moderation
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="122" y="462" text-anchor="middle">
    abuse classifiers
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="122" y="480" text-anchor="middle">
    copyright fingerprint match
  </text>

  <line class="dg-line" x1="236" y1="454" x2="266" y2="454"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="276,454 266,449 266,459"></polygon>

  <!-- One transition, and everything outside this group is invisible -->
  <rect class="dg-group" x="276" y="386" width="416" height="118"></rect>
  <text class="dg-legend" x="286" y="410">Live to viewers</text>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="292" y="420" width="176" height="68"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="380" y="442" text-anchor="middle">Publish</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="380" y="460" text-anchor="middle"
    >state: published</text
  >
  <text class="dg-sub" x="380" y="478" text-anchor="middle">
    first moment it is visible
  </text>

  <line class="dg-line" x1="468" y1="454" x2="492" y2="454"></line>
  <polygon class="dg-head" points="500,454 490,449 490,459"></polygon>

  <rect class="dg-box" x="500" y="420" width="176" height="68"></rect>
  <text class="dg-label" x="588" y="442" text-anchor="middle">CDN</text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="588" y="460" text-anchor="middle">
    pulled on the first view
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sub" x="588" y="478" text-anchor="middle">
    nothing is pushed
  </text>
</Figure>
